-- title:
--   Constant stalk rank (p-1)deg g of the level ring
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime (also assumed nonzero as a natural number), let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$ for the divisors $d$ of $p$, and let `Afin p` be the finite-$j$ chart algebra $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `chartAlg` of $F$ attached to the element $j \in F$ of the two-chart integral model. Assume the Laurent series $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$, i.e. `modularUnitSeries p` (the product of `deltaSeries` with the inverse of its $p$-fold $q$-substitute), lies in $F$, and let $v \in$ `Afin p` be an element whose image in $F$ is either this series or $p^{12}$ times its inverse. Let $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ be monic with $g(0) \neq 0$, and let $c$ be a nonzero integer. Consider the level ring $B =$ `levelRing p c v g`, the quotient of the localisation of `Afin p` away from $c$ by the principal ideal generated by $g$ evaluated at the image of $v$. Assuming $B$ is a finite and flat module over $\mathbb{Z}[1/c] =$ `Localization.Away c`, the conclusion is that for every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $\mathbb{Z}[1/c]$ the rank of $B$ at the stalk at $\mathfrak{q}$ equals $(p-1)\cdot \deg g$ (natural-number subtraction and degree).
--
--   This is the rank computation for the level sets of the modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{p})$ (and its Fricke transform $p^{12}\Delta(q^p)/\Delta(q)$) on the finite-$j$ chart of the integral model of $X_0(p)$, the degree $p-1$ being that of the divisor of this unit. It supplies the rank clause of [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_self`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_self).
-- source:
